.TH qsh-service-install 1  "install 0.4.3" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-service\-install \- Write (or rewrite) the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode and create its parent directories. Without `\-\-activate` nothing is started
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh service install\fR [\fB\-\-activate\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write (or rewrite) the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode and create its parent directories. Without `\-\-activate` nothing is started
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-activate\fR
Also load and start the unit through the service manager (`launchctl bootstrap` / `systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now` / `schtasks /Create` then `/Run`) once the unit file is written. A unit that is already running is not restarted, so a new binary path applies at the next restart
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.4.3
